// title: Validate before you deploy
// date: 2026-11-12
// product: Sentinel
// tables: W3CIISLog
// purpose: From the article: KQL Detection of the Week: Two Things Called SharePoint
// source: https://devsecopsdadattack.com/2026-11-12-KQL-Detection-of-the-Week-Two-Things-Called-SharePoint/
// kind: article
// author: DevSecOpsDad · DevSecOpsDad (detection engineering briefs, KQL)
// archived by tools/kql_archive.py (CLAUDE.md 5l, 5eu)
// 1. Are you collecting IIS logs from the farm at all?
//    An empty Sites column usually just means IIS isn't logging the
//    "Service Name" (s-sitename) field, which is off by default.
W3CIISLog
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(1d)
| summarize Requests = count(), Sites = make_set(sSiteName, 10) by Computer
